 105:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   */
 106:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c **** 
 107:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c **** /** @defgroup HAL_Exported_Functions_Group1 Initialization and de-initialization Functions 
 108:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****  *  @brief    Initialization and de-initialization functions
 109:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****  *
 110:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c **** @verbatim    
 111:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****  ===============================================================================
 112:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****               ##### Initialization and Configuration functions #####
 113:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****  ===============================================================================
 114:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****     [..]  This section provides functions allowing to:
 115:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****       (+) Initializes the Flash interface the NVIC allocation and initial clock 
 116:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****           configuration. It initializes the systick also when timeout is needed 
 117:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****           and the backup domain when enabled.
 118:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****       (+) De-Initializes common part of the HAL.
 119:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****       (+) Configure the time base source to have 1ms time base with a dedicated 
 120:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****           Tick interrupt priority. 
 121:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****         (++) SysTick timer is used by default as source of time base, but user
 122:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              can eventually implement his proper time base source (a general purpose 
 123:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              timer for example or other time source), keeping in mind that Time base 
 124:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              duration should be kept 1ms since PPP_TIMEOUT_VALUEs are defined and 
 125:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              handled in milliseconds basis.
 126:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****         (++) Time base configuration function (HAL_InitTick ()) is called automatically 
 127:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              at the beginning of the program after reset by HAL_Init() or at any time 
 128:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              when clock is configured, by HAL_RCC_ClockConfig(). 
 129:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****         (++) Source of time base is configured  to generate interrupts at regular 
 130:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              time intervals. Care must be taken if HAL_Delay() is called from a 
 131:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              peripheral ISR process, the Tick interrupt line must have higher priority 
 132:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****             (numerically lower) than the peripheral interrupt. Otherwise the caller 
 133:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****             ISR process will be blocked. 
 134:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****        (++) functions affecting time base configurations are declared as __weak  
 135:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****              to make  override possible  in case of other  implementations in user file.
 136:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c **** @endverbatim
 137:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   * @{
 138:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   */
 139:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c **** 
 140:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c **** /**
 141:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   * @brief  This function is used to initialize the HAL Library; it must be the first 
 142:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *         instruction to be executed in the main program (before to call any other
 143:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *         HAL function), it performs the following:
 144:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *           Configure the Flash prefetch, instruction and Data caches.
 145:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *           Configures the SysTick to generate an interrupt each 1 millisecond,
 146:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *           which is clocked by the HSI (at this stage, the clock is not yet
 147:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *           configured and thus the system is running from the internal HSI at 16 MHz).
 148:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *           Set NVIC Group Priority to 4.
 149:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *           Calls the HAL_MspInit() callback function defined in user file 
 150:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal.c ****   *           "stm32f4xx_hal_msp.c" to do the global low level hardware initialization 
